<Layout
  title={`${NAME} — the box set`}
  description="A free, open source music app for Plex, Jellyfin and Navidrome, drawn as a boxed piece of 1994 consumer electronics. Everything is in the one box — because every feature is in the free app."
  themeColor="#f7ede0"
  noindex
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link
      href="https://api.fontshare.com/v2/css?f[]=clash-display@600,700&f[]=satoshi@400,500,700,900&f[]=khand@500,600,700&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </Fragment>

  <main class="bx">
    <!--
      THESIS: Mozz as a boxed 1994 consumer-electronics product. Everything the app
      does comes in the one carton — the physical argument for "every feature is in
      the free app, there is no paid tier". The hero is one massive knolling shot of
      the box's entire contents; every later section is another printed part of the
      package (back-of-box requirements, a spec panel, the manual, the warranty card,
      the quick-start fold).
      OWN-WORLD: Warm cream table with un-erased construction lines; flat screen-print
      colour, one hard value step per face; printed-carton detail — barcodes, edge
      fluting on cut board, die-cut sticker sheets, moulded tray recesses with lit
      draft angles. Kraft tan + slate blue over cream, brand red for the marks.
      DROP-IN: /hero/boxset.jpg layers over the drawing and degrades to nothing.
    -->

    <VariantBar slug="boxset" tone="warm" />

    <!-- HERO ---------------------------------------------------------------- -->
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="lockup">
          <Mark size={26} decorative />
          <span class="wordmark">{NAME}</span>
          <span class="lockup-tick">model m-01 · one box</span>
